2026-01-30 10:30:50 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-30 10:30:50 | OUTPUT |     Joke 2 is more directly tied to the headline. The framing of China being upset about Panama "exchanging numbers" with Taiwan is clever and plays on the idea of a jealous relationship. The back-and-forth dialogue, with Panama's defensive response about a "fact-finding mission on semiconductor trade," adds to the humor and feels more natural. It's also more concise and doesn't explain itself. The "overreacting" line is a nice touch. It feels more like a natural reaction someone might actually have.
2026-01-30 10:30:50 | OUTPUT |     
2026-01-30 10:30:50 | OUTPUT |     Joke 1 feels a little forced in its attempt to be funny, while Joke 2 feels more organic and directly addresses the core issue in a witty way. Joke 2 also benefits from the conversational format, which lends itself well to a quick, punchy joke.
